; docs/semantics/kinds/deffact.eadl — the kind the capability vocabulary is written with.
;
; ROADMAP.md §5.3 asks for a "versioned capability vocabulary", and §5.2 for "a documented comparison
; direction" for every parameter the engine compares. `docs/decisions/decision_substitutability-relation.md`
; §1.1 decides both: every fact the relation judges is one `deffact` entry of
; `docs/semantics/vocabulary/vocabulary.eadl`, which fixes the fact's value kind, whom it speaks for, and which
; way an offered value must lie against a required one.
;
; ⭐ DECLARED WITH `defkind`, LIKE EVERY OTHER KIND. So `deffact` is no more privileged than a kind a user adds
; (reference §7 rule 1), and it carries no behaviour (§7 rule 3): its clauses hold names, lists of names and one
; line of text, and nothing that could be run. The rules that compute a derived fact are engine knowledge in
; `crates/eadl-resolve`, each named here by its `rule` clause and listed in the record's §4.
;
; ⛔ NO DESCRIPTION'S REGISTRY HOLDS THIS KIND. The shipped registry is `core.eadl` and `os-rt.eadl`
; (`crates/archogen-api/src/lib.rs`'s `KIND_MODULES`), so a `deffact` inside a module is `schema-unknown-kind`.
; Any other file that writes one is the language's own definition and not a description, and `archogen check`
; answers it as it answers a kind module (record §1.1, `SR-H3`). `crates/eadl-resolve` registers this kind to
; validate the vocabulary with `kind.rs`'s `validate`, and reads the entries into its typed table (leaf
; `M3.1.2.2`), which checks what a frame cannot: that `implies` is written only on a set fact, that no fact is
; named like a clause word, and that `derived-from` and `reads` close no cycle.
;
; THE CLAUSES, as the record's §1.1 table states them:
;
;   doc           what the fact means, one line; required, as a kind's `doc` is
;   domain        its value kind: `boolean`; `count`; `quantity <dimension>`; `interval <dimension>`;
;                 `enumeration <symbol>…`, or `enumeration (ordered <symbol>…)` for a total order, lowest
;                 first; `set <symbol>…`; `group <fact>…`
;   role          `guarantee`, a promise the offer makes; or `statement`, the requiring side's word about itself
;   direction     `at-least`, `at-most`, `exact`, `includes` or `within`: how an offered value satisfies a
;                 required one
;   derived-from  the facts a derivation computes this one from, when it is not offered directly
;   reads         the optional inputs the rule reads beside `derived-from`'s required ones
;   rule          the engine's rule that computes it
;   implies       for a set fact, the members every valued constraint on it holds beside what it writes

(eadl-version eadl/1)

(defkind deffact
  (doc "a fact of the capability vocabulary: its value kind, whom it speaks for, and which way an offered value satisfies a required one")
  (name required)
  (clause doc (cardinality one) (holds values string))
  (clause domain (cardinality one) (holds forms))
  (clause role (cardinality one) (holds values symbol))
  (clause direction (cardinality one) (holds values symbol))
  (clause derived-from (cardinality at-most-one) (holds forms))
  (clause reads (cardinality at-most-one) (holds forms))
  (clause rule (cardinality at-most-one) (holds values symbol))
  (clause implies (cardinality at-most-one) (holds forms)))
